{
  "name": "pre-read-after-a-shell-only-recovery-and-a-peer-commit-is-denied",
  "description": "#514: a recovery the shell used up does not admit a later stale Read. A reads v1 and B commits v2, which makes A's copy INVALID; A's Read of the v2 bytes B committed is denied, which arms A's recovery. A then recovers through the shell alone: its `cat plan.md` is denied and re-grants SHARED (fixture 11), and the retry runs and reads v2 (fixture 13). B commits v3. A's Read of the v3 bytes is denied with the commit text, its one deny for this stale copy; prior_version_seen_by_session is 2, the version the retried `cat` read. Before the fix the recovery the first deny armed was still set, so this Read was admitted with no deny on either backend. The next Read is admitted (fixture 44). Timestamps vary per run; the reason bytes and the summary are the contract.",
